Drives runtime/gc/gc.bit's pointer-map VALIDATION with a deliberately malformed
TypeInfo, counting bad offsets in gcStatBadOffsets. It exercises the collector's
own validation path directly rather than through a safepoint, and its @nosplit
runtime code cannot poll; the host collector running is beside the point here.

`BIT_GC=stress` does not report zero, though: 5/5 runs measured
`collections=101`, matching stress.bit's own documented scheduler-loop floor
(runtime/sched/workerrun.bit's `Worker.run`, which every worker OS thread
keeps running regardless of what this program does). None of those 101 pass
through this program's own `@nosplit` validation code, so the collection count
remains beside the point for the reason already stated.
